Z||000000||fieromillie||06-10-2001||12:54 AM||||Hi Everyone,<BR>You guys were so helpfull before I thought I would seek some help again. My 84 Ebay Michigan Fiero is now not shifting all the time. Problem is getting so bad. Cant even go a mile without it happening. The clutch will suddenly have no pressure behind it. Goes to the floor and then I cannot shift gears at all. I get if off the road and it eventually will build back up only to take off and then do it again. Today I managed to get it into a parking lot and turned the key off and then I could put it in Neutral but there was still no clutch and being on a incline it acted as thoe it was in first gear. I was surprised when it didnt drift. Usually in neutral on a incline it would. Any suggestions would be appreciated. Thanks so much, Ann     ||||reg||9
Z||000001||KissMySSFiero||06-10-2001||01:10 AM||||sounds to me like a clutch slave cylinder.  <P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>      <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>       <P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">           <BR>"Kids in the backseat cause accidents,  accidents in the backseat caused me!!"||||reg||1
Z||000002||isthiswhereiputausername?||06-10-2001||11:17 AM||||Did you check the fluid in the clutch slave cylinder? also get someone to stand beside the car when you try to shift and see if anything moves down by the transmission... I had a bracket broken on mine before causing my 4sp to shift bad.<P><BR>hope everything works out good for you and the car after you get these bugs worked out..<BR>sounded like the last owner knew nothing about fieros.<P><BR>||||reg||1
